-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CCFULL-ROM training input (python -m emulator.train_global, python -m
emulator.train_local).  The lines are read in order; blank lines and lines
starting with # are skipped, and nothing after the dashed line is read.  Paths
are relative to the project root.

 1-9  CCFULL input of the reaction (ccfull.inp of physical_model/ccfull_clean).
      Line 3 is the rotor record E2T,beta2,beta4,beta6,NrotT, and its six
      parameters with those of line 7 are the nominal point.  CCFULL at the
      nominal point puts r_min at the bottom of its pocket; the training keeps
      this r_min for every parameter point (line 10 of ccfull.inp), so that all
      snapshots share one radial grid.
 10   system name, the first part of both model names.  The rest of each name
      is written from the settings:
        global: <system>_Global_Channel<channels>_Snap<snapshots>_POD<rank>_EIM<modes>
        local:  <system>_Local_Channel<channels>_Snap<snapshots>_POD<rank>_EIM<modes>
      with the snapshots and rank of line 16 (global) or 19 (local, per (E, J)),
      and the CC-EIM modes of line 17, e.g.
      34S_168Er_Local_Channel6_Snap300_POD80_EIM40.  The channels are NrotT + 1
      of line 3.  Each model is written to training_root/<name>; a training
      stops if that folder exists.
 11   experimental data file of this reaction.
 12   training_root: folder of the trained models.
 13   bounds of beta2, beta4, beta6: lower,upper of each.  Equal bounds fix
      a parameter, e.g. 0.0,0.0 for beta6.
 14   bounds of V0 (MeV), r0 (fm), a0 (fm), as line 13.
 15   energy range of the global model; any energy inside it can be emulated.
      experimental: the measured energies of line 11, rounded outward to MeV.
      ccfull: Emin and Emax of line 8.  Or lower,upper in MeV, e.g. 52.0,100.0.
 16   global model: snapshots, basis rank, seed.  The snapshots are
      Latin-hypercube points in (beta2, beta4, beta6, V0, r0, a0, E, u): one run
      of the interface program each, of which the partial wave J is taken by u
      among those CCFULL solved.  The basis keeps that many POD modes of them,
      and each online (E, J) solve is a rank x rank system.
 17   CC-EIM of the coupling field: parameter points (potential evaluations
      only), seed, number of modes.  All independent elements of the coupling
      matrix are interpolated together and the leading POD modes are kept.
      The training prints the interpolation error at new parameter points, so
      the number of modes can be chosen from it.
 18   energies of the local model: none, experimental (the measured energies of
      line 11), or first,last,step in MeV.  The local model is trained
      separately from the global model: one small basis per (E, J) from its own
      runs of the interface program, and its own CC-EIM with the settings of
      line 17.  It is several times faster than the global model but emulates
      only these energies.
 19   local model: basis vectors per (E, J), Latin-hypercube points, seed.
      Every energy is solved at the same points and at the corners of the box;
      the block of a partial wave uses the runs in which CCFULL solved it, so the
      highest partial waves have fewer snapshots and a smaller basis.
